#: processes/ig-incremental-build.bpmn:284
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "A preview never seeds the shared cache."
msgstr ""

#: processes/ig-incremental-build.bpmn:101
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "A push to a PR branch (review path) or to main / a release (publish path). Both run this process; only the publish path may seed the cache."
msgstr ""

#: processes/ig-incremental-build.bpmn:197
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Answered by Task_Validate — the cone's resources checked against the warm validator. `yes` goes on to re-render the cone's records. `no` logs the findings on the change's bean and returns them to the author. A validator that could not start is could-not-determine, which Task_Validate's documentation says is never a pass, so it does not take `yes`; and a green cone is not a green IG, since a profile the change did not touch can still be broken by it."
msgstr ""

#: processes/ig-incremental-build.bpmn:113
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Answered by the exit code of `ig-cache restore` (Task_Restore): 0 is a usable cache and takes `yes`, into the cone machinery. 1 (a miss) or 3 (present, but the toolchain moved) takes `no`, to the full publisher build, whose outputs become the records the next seed writes. Exit 2 (an environment error — the cache could not be read, which says nothing about whether it is usable) takes `environment error`: the run stops and the error is logged, rather than falling back to a full build that would hide a broken cache store behind a slow green run."
msgstr ""

#: processes/ig-incremental-build.bpmn:278
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Answered by the push that started the process. `PR branch` is the review path: deploy the preview, which never seeds the shared cache. `main / release` is the publish path: deploy the site after a human has authorised the release, then seed the cache, which writes to a -test branch, verifies a restore from a clean clone, and only then promotes. Only this branch reaches the lane allowed to touch the shared cache."
msgstr ""

#: processes/ig-incremental-build.bpmn:242
#. Diagram label
msgid "Assemble the site (template · Jekyll) [ig-publication]"
msgstr ""

#: processes/ig-incremental-build.bpmn:243
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Assemble the site from the merged records: the IG template and a Jekyll build over output/. Only site assembly happens here — every artefact record already exists."
msgstr ""

